#. Key:	76F8DCAB40AFB41DBE490C94BF5D3DD7
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_0.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_0.Help Text
msgctxt ",76F8DCAB40AFB41DBE490C94BF5D3DD7"
msgid "Two impact systems are available:\r\nA Niagara Data Channel is used to pass multiple impacts to a single emitter [1]. \r\nAlternatively you can spawn an individual system for each impact [2].\r\n\r\nPhysics materials are used to vary the look of each impact.\r\n\r\nLine Trace [L] or Projectile [P] impacts can be used."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	51107015440E56E291DCB0995FE273AA
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_1.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_1.Help Text
msgctxt ",51107015440E56E291DCB0995FE273AA"
msgid "Welcome to the Niagara Examples Gallery\r\n\r\nThis level showcases the VFX systems included in the Niagara Examples Pack.\r\n\r\nYou can use the systems as is or adapt them to fit your needs.\r\n\r\nPress H to open the documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	420C80E24AFDD60D15C393A2F6D189E4
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_2.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_2.Help Text
msgctxt ",420C80E24AFDD60D15C393A2F6D189E4"
msgid "Explosions [3, 4, 5] use a physics field to impart force on impact.\r\n\r\nPhysics materials on the disks are used to trigger dirt explosions rather than the default."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	3F4497C346F58AF815BAA0B55357292E
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_3.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_3.Help Text
msgctxt ",3F4497C346F58AF815BAA0B55357292E"
msgid "A Tesla Coil is a fun use case for our NE_Arc emitter example.  As you enter the range, you become the target.  This uses a few of our examples to achive the overall result.  \r\nRefer to the BP_TeslaCoil setup for details."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	343BDCE54EA023DA035C4D834BFF7AE8
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_4.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_4.Help Text
msgctxt ",343BDCE54EA023DA035C4D834BFF7AE8"
msgid "The colored spheres in the distance will react to explosion impacts [3, 4, 5].\r\n\r\nUse the projectile mode [P] for an extra challenge!"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	11585962421F63510F9716A43B3134BF
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_5.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_5.Help Text
msgctxt ",11585962421F63510F9716A43B3134BF"
msgid "Impact decals attach to moving targets.\r\n\r\nIf the NDC impact system is being used a single NDC system is attached per hit component. Subsequent impacts are handled by the previously attached system.\r\n\r\nIn Line Trace mode one system is spawned per impact. Each system is attached to the hit component. Decal emitters are in local space. Other dust/debris emitters are in world space."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	318CF2D74230E11D3B7AE49895F2F2B0
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_6.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_6.Help Text
msgctxt ",318CF2D74230E11D3B7AE49895F2F2B0"
msgid "The included animations contain animation notify events for each footstep.\r\n\r\nA simple version of the animation notify blueprint can be found in the FX_Footprint folder.\r\n\r\nA version specific to this gallery character can be found in the Gallery/Blueprints folder.\r\n\r\nNiagara Data Channel and Spawned systems are both supported."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	4E8B9656456F317EA0E170BC053350C9
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_7.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_7.Help Text
msgctxt ",4E8B9656456F317EA0E170BC053350C9"
msgid "Impacts apply a physics impulse along the hit direction, causing physics bodies to react when hit."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	A3D4DC8549BF19C7D18C99AB34A65F25
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_8.Help Text
#: /Game/NiagaraExamples/GalleryLevel.GalleryLevel:PersistentLevel.BP_HelpStand_C_8.Help Text
msgctxt ",A3D4DC8549BF19C7D18C99AB34A65F25"
msgid "This gallery is 1,000,000 units from the origin. Use it to confirm that your FX assets behave as you would expect.\r\n\r\nLarge World Coordinates (LWC): Niagara uses a tile+offset scheme when handling very large coordinates. A tile is roughly 260,000 units in size by default. As systems and/or particles cross this threshold make sure the behavior is expected.\r\n\r\nScalability: Distance from the player is a common metric used to cull or skip spawning systems. Environment assets can sometimes trigger errors if systems are not spawned due to scalability yet code attempts to modify those systems without checking validity first."
msgstr ""

